From b3e8a2d8241dc23d6c1bcd838ce7f3d48dd8beb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:43:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gguf: DeepSeek-V4.1 from a GGUF pack, the format on tier 0

The pieces a GGUF pack needs that stand on tier 0 alone: the dense weights read
from a "deepseek41" GGUF under the checkpoint's own names (KT_GGUF_V41_DENSE,
kt_gguf_dense_v41), the GGUF wo_a (MMQ, dequant + GEMM, or one MoE-vector launch),
the GGUF quant config next to expert_pack, the GPU hot experts as raw GGUF blocks
(kt_gguf_hot, kt_gguf_moe_multi with llama.cpp's vec-dot headers copied from
SGLang by setup.sh), the GGUF dequantizers, and the SM75 paths (Triton e4m3 and
fp32 dots below SM80/89, bf16 kept with KT_SM75_BF16).

Nothing here runs for the MXFP4 checkpoint: the loader, the hot method and the
RoPE rows take a GGUF pack only (KT_GGUF_V41_DENSE, kt_config.method LLAMAFILE),
the SM75 branches are capability checks. The RoPE rows past KT_ROPE_DEVICE_ROWS
go to host memory only with tier 1's kv-vmm; without it the table stays on the
GPU.
